ps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T19:19:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T19:19:33Z","body":"Working on a separate ToolScript fix (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116368), and played with this MRP. This appears to have 3 issues going on:\n1. The ToolScript isn't being hard-reloaded which produces inconsistencies in the exported variables \n2. Having an `@onready` Variable inside a `@tool` Script produces inconsistencies, the ScriptInstance is only readied once and of course doesn't change when properties are changed\n3. Having a `set()` in a tool function, which processes before `@onready` due to validate_properties being called before ready (well-pointed out earlier in thread) - https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113283\n\nFrom what I can tell, testing with my ToolScript fix improves the behavior in this case, but does not resolve all of it because of the `@onready` code structure.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910195939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"